                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is a strategy puzzle game which combines both time and resource management.  The story is about Claire, a historian and archeologist at a prominent university.  One day Claire finds a map showing there is treasure in the lands of the ancient Tonauak tribe, so she embarks on a long journey with a small team in order to find this treasure before any other archeologists do.\r\n\r\nHowever, a dark priest has stolen a mysterious ancient relic so that he can perform a ritual which will give him both immortality and unlimited power.  In the process, he will destroy everything the tribe holds dear.  Thus, Claire and her team are now put to the test in a race against time as they try to save the tribe by overcoming the dark magic of the priest and thwarting his evil plans.\r\n\r\nThe Store Page says there are 40 levels to beat, but there are actually 49, and each one has a timer on it.  Of course, the missions get progressively harder and harder.  You must do tasks like gather food, chop wood, forge iron, mine gold, chase off thieves, relocate bee hives, and rebuild totems.  At the beginning of each level you will be told what specific tasks must be done for that level.\r\n\r\nEach task will take resources.  Some tasks will create resources, and some will give back resources.  For some levels, you start out with a limited number of resources, and there are multiple paths you can take.  You must choose your path carefully, or you will run out of a specific resource and thus fail the level.  Pay attention to the list of tasks which are your objectives for the level.\r\n\r\nFor example, just because you can upgrade a building does not mean you should.  Doing so might take scarce resources that are needed somewhere else.  You must think very fast, knowing which resources to deploy, and in which order to deploy them, so that you can reach the objective.  Also, you must do all of this while chasing off resource thieves, and watching the timer count down.\r\n\r\nThe game has 2D cartoon graphics.  It should take you between 10 to 15 hours to complete the game and get all of the achievements.  Also, the achievements DO count on your Profile.  However, there are neither trading cards nor Point Shop items.  The game ran perfectly fine too.  I experienced no bugs or glitches.  This game was a good exercise for the brain.  I must find more like this one.",
